    "problem_statement": "Assign operation returns wrong value and has broken argument handling\n\n#### Description\n\nThe `Assign` operation is not working correctly - it's returning the assigned value instead of the target, and there seem to be issues with argument ordering in the internal implementation.\n\n#### Steps/Code to Reproduce\n\n```python\nfrom glom import glom, Assign, T\n\n# Basic assignment should return the modified target, not the assigned value\ntarget = {}\nresult = glom(target, Assign(T['a'], 1))\nprint(\"Expected: {'a': 1}\")\nprint(\"Actual:\", result)\n\n# More complex case\nclass Foo:\n    pass\n\nfoo_obj = Foo()\nresult = glom(foo_obj, Assign(T.a, 1))\nprint(\"Expected: Foo object with .a = 1\")\nprint(\"Actual:\", result)\nprint(\"Type:\", type(result))\n```\n\nThe assignment operations are failing because the function is returning the assigned value instead of the target object. This breaks the expected behavior where `Assign` should modify the target and return it."
  }
